  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Secret Guard for DSH",
      "text": "> Local-only credential scan and redaction for prompts, logs, diffs, and files. Findings are\n> redacted; the full secret is never returned."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\nnode bin/dsh-secret-guard.mjs --file notes.txt\ncat notes.txt | node bin/dsh-secret-guard.mjs --redact\n```\n\nIn DSH:\n\n```text\nUse secret_scan on this text.\nUse secret_redact before sharing this file.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Rules",
      "text": "GitHub tokens, AWS keys, OpenAI-style keys, private-key blocks, JWT-like tokens, and assigned\ncredential values."
    },
    {
      "section": "Limits",
      "text": "- Pattern-based, not entropy/AST/secret-manager integration.\n- A clean scan is not proof that a document is secret-free.\n- Redaction can break syntax; review the result.\n- No network, no telemetry, no write to disk."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\nTest tokens are constructed at runtime; no real credential is committed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Provenance",
      "text": "A small independent scanner. Inspired by common secret-scanning practice; no source copied.\nLicense: MIT."
    }
  ],
